eceived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think those errors should be kept. The checks for `p_polygon.size() < 3` should likely be done outside of these functions.\r\n\r\nIn general, you have to think the same for all functions: if the function does not do what you would expect it should do, it should throw an error. So here, if `add_polygon` or ` set_polygon` do not add/set the provided polygon, the functions should throw an error. It's up to the caller of those functions to check the arguments before calling the function.","created_at":"2026-01-08T09:11:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-08T09:11:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114278#discussion_r2671536587","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114278","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2671536587"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114278#discussion_r2671536587"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114278"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2671536587/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":821,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2673373959","pull_request_review_id":3640631039,"id":2673373959,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6fWHMH","diff_hunk":"@@ -7014,7 +7021,7 @@ void TileData::_get_property_list(List<PropertyInfo> *p_list) const {\n \t\t\tfor (int j = 0; j < physics[i].polygons.size(); j++) {\n \t\t\t\t// physics_layer_%d/points\n \t\t\t\tproperty_info = PropertyInfo(Variant::ARRAY, vformat(\"physics_layer_%d/polygon_%d/%s\", i, j, PNAME(\"points\")), PROPERTY_HINT